<title>BELGIUM: EU clears Danish/Swedish dairy joint venture.</title>
<headline>EU clears Danish/Swedish dairy joint venture.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission cleared on Tuesday the creation of a joint venture by Danish dairy cooperative MD Foods Amba and Sweden's Arla after changes were made to address European Union competition concerns.</p>
<p>The venture, Scandairy K/S, will be active in the dairy sector, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The parties had agreed to limit the venture's sphere of activity after the EU executive initially expressed serious doubts about its compability with antitrust rules.</p>
<p>The Commission said its concerns had been met by the changes, which limits the cooperation to a fast-growing food sector where major research and development investments are required.</p>
<p>But it added that it would re-examine the deal after seven years.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom +32 2 287 68 11</p>
